    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i spent fifteen years building my research... every waking hour was dedicated to finding some kind of signal in the noise. and i finally realized there is no signal. it was all just noise. i look at my work now and i don't even see myself in it. i just see a massive waste of time. it's like i've been running a race for a finish line that doesn't even exist. i'm just so tired of trying to find meaning where there isn't any.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
